---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import CrossLinks from '../components/CrossLinks.astro';
import Needs from '../components/Needs.astro';
import Draft from '../components/Draft.astro';
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="Dealer-network monitoring for a technical support persona"
  metaTitle="Field operations — data-dense B2B dashboards | Tyler Young"
  description="Dealer-network monitoring built for a technical support persona, with an AI layer that answers what needs my attention."
  descriptionDraft
  eyebrow="Data-Dense B2B"
  meta={[
    ['Contribution', '[NEEDS: Tyler’s line — what he owned here]'],
    ['Role', '[NEEDS: role and dates]'],
    ['Scope', 'Dashboards, metric cards, AI attention surface'],
    ['Attribution', 'Atheer engagement'],
    ['Status', 'Blocked on a decision about what can be shown'],
  ]}
>
  <div class="aside">
    <p>
      This page is a shell. Nothing here ships until Tyler decides which screens can
      be public. If none can, the homepage card becomes text-only or is cut — that is
      his call, not a default.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Why this is on the site</h2>
  <p>
    <Draft>
      Everything else visible here is consumer commerce. This is the one surface that
      looks like the software a technical buyer actually works in: dense tables, live
      metrics, a support persona who is monitoring rather than browsing.
    </Draft>
  </p>

  <h2>The problem</h2>
  <p>
    <Needs>
      Tyler's framing — what the support persona was actually trying to do, and what
      made it hard
    </Needs>
  </p>

  <h2>The AI attention layer</h2>
  <p>
    <Draft>
      A dashboard that shows everything shows nothing. The design question was not how
      to display more signal, it was how to answer one question on arrival: what needs
      my attention right now.
    </Draft>
  </p>
  <p>
    <Needs>
      Tyler's account of how the attention feature actually worked, and what it ranked
      on. No invented mechanics.
    </Needs>
  </p>

  <div class="shot">
    <Needs block ratio="16 / 9">
      Dashboard overview — the highest-value screen, if it can be shown
    </Needs>
  </div>

  <div class="shot">
    <Needs block ratio="16 / 9">
      Metric cards and the "what needs my attention" surface
    </Needs>
  </div>

  <h2>Outcome</h2>
  <p>
    <Needs>3–5 real, verifiable statements — or cut this section entirely</Needs>
  </p>

  <CrossLinks
    slot="after"
    label="Related"
    title="How this work gets built now"
    links={[
      { href: '/atheer-design-pipeline', label: 'The design-to-code pipeline' },
      { href: '/how-i-design-with-ai', label: 'How I design with AI' },
    ]}
  />
</DocumentLayout>

<style>
  .shot {
    margin: 0 0 26px;
  }
</style>
